 Open sessions are not held across view rendering (`spring.jpa.open-in-view` is disabled), so associations that a view needs are fetched eagerly at the mapping level.
 
+## Scale and Load
+
+This section lists each code path whose cost grows with stored data, and the form chosen for it. Every path recorded so far is bounded and uses the simplest readable form. A size no human has supplied is written as unrecorded and treated as bounded; the seed data gives the only observed figure.
+
+| Path | Dominant operations | Realistic size | Access pattern | Form |
+|------|---------------------|----------------|----------------|------|
+| Visit booking and correction (`VisitController`) | One owner lookup by identity loading the whole owner graph; linear scans of that owner's pets and of one pet's visits | Seed data: at most two pets per owner and two visits per pet. Production size unrecorded, treated as bounded | One request per form open or submit | Simplest readable form: in-memory scan of the loaded collections, O(pets + visits) worst-case |
+
 ## Dependency Policy
 
 Minimize external dependencies. Every dependency is an attack surface and a maintenance burden.
